{title: 199 - The Head That Once Was Crowned}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]The [G/B]head [A/C#]that [D]once [D7/C]was [G/B]crowned [D]with [G]thorns
[D]Is [G]crowned with [Em]glory [D]now;
[D]A [G]royal [D7]diadem [C]adorns
[D7/C]The [Bm]mighty [C]victor's [D7]brow.

Verse 2:
[D]The highest [A/C#]place [D]that [D7/C]heaven [D]affords
[D]Is [G]His, is [Em]His [Am]by [D]right;
[D]The [G]King [D7]of [Em]kings, [Bm]and [C]Lord [A/C#]of [D]lords,
[D7/C]And [Bm]heaven's [C]eternal [G]light.

Verse 3:
[D]The [G/B]joy [A/C#]of [D]all [D7/C]who [G/B]dwell [D]above,
[D]The [G]joy of [Em]all [Am]below,
[D]To [G]whom [D7]He [Em]manifests [A/C#]His [D]love,
[D7/C]And [Bm]grants [C]His name [G/D]to [D7]know.

Verse 4:
[D]To [G/B]them [A/C#]the [D]cross, [D7/C]with [G/B]all [D]its [G]shame,
[D]With all [G]its grace [Em]is [Am]given;
[D]Their [G]name [D7]an [Em]everlasting [D]name,
[D7/C]Their [Bm]joy [C]the joy [G/D]of [D7]heaven.
